jess: Hey — repro in our Expo sample app after the SDK bump. Bundle fails with missing polyfills and then the auth layer gets into a retry loop. Anyone seen this?

sam: paste the error?

jess: Metro error: "Unable to resolve module 'stream' from 'node_modules/redwood-sdk/dist/index.js'". Full stack: 
```
Error: Unable to resolve module `stream` from `.../node_modules/redwood-sdk/dist/index.js`: stream could not be found within the project.
    at ResolutionRequest.resolveDependency (...)
```

kevin: that's the classic node core libs issue. Metro doesn't supply node core by default. Two quick routes: add node-libs-react-native or map required modules to RN-friendly polyfills via extraNodeModules.

kevin: example metro.config.js we used in another app:
```
const path = require('path');
module.exports = {
  resolver: {
    extraNodeModules: {
      stream: require.resolve('readable-stream'),
      crypto: require.resolve('react-native-quick-crypto'),
      buffer: require.resolve('buffer/'),
    },
  },
};
```

maria: also for randomness on RN you need `react-native-get-random-values` (import it at the app entry). Some of the SDK code expects `crypto.getRandomValues`.

maria: add to App.js: `import 'react-native-get-random-values';` and install `react-native-quick-crypto` if you need webcrypto-like APIs.

jess: did that — bundle succeeded but now auth is weird. After login we get a 401 and the SDK retries indefinitely, so user sees repeated sign-in prompts. Logs: 
```
[auth] request failed 401 -> retrying (attempt 3)
[auth] request failed 401 -> retrying (attempt 4)
```

sam: ah hmm. The SDK's retry policy treats any non-2xx as retriable right now. That's bad for 401. We should only retry on network errors and 5xx.

sam: quick patch idea (pseudo):
```
if (response.status === 401) {
  // auth error: don't retry, surface to caller
  throw new AuthError();
}
if (status >= 500) {
  // retryable server error
  retry();
}
```

kevin: agreed. Also expose a config flag like `retryOnAuthError: false` so enterprise apps can override. We should also log the original 401 body to help debugging.

maria: FYI typing issue too: our TS types reference `ReadableStream` / `Blob` from DOM which RN doesn't have. Sample app fell over with `Cannot find name 'ReadableStream'`. Workarounds: add `lib: ['esnext']` + ambient declarations, or add a tiny `global.d.ts` in the sample app: `declare type ReadableStream = any; declare var Blob: any;`

jess: hmm adding `dom` to tsconfig caused other conflicts for RN. I like the `global.d.ts` approach for the sample app. I'll include a comment to remove it for web builds.

maria: also update the README onboarding: mention metro config, the two polyfills, and the `global.d.ts` snippet. That should reduce friction for new RN integrators.

jess: i'll open a PR that: (1) updates the Expo sample to import `react-native-get-random-values`, adds metro.extraNodeModules mapping, (2) adds global.d.ts for ReadableStream/Blob, (3) adjusts SDK retry logic to not retry on 401 and expose `retryOnAuthError` option, and (4) adds a short note in onboarding docs.

dev-bot: Issue created automatically -> #5234: "expo sample: bundle polyfills + auth retry + types fixes". Assigned to jess.

sam: thanks. If you want I can review the retry patch. Quick test plan: repro login failure -> confirm no retry on 401 -> confirm 5xx still retries -> test expo dev and production bundles.

jess: awesome, i'll land a small patch and ping you. Cheers :thumbsup:
